  "narrative": {
    "intro": "BL Harbert International has obligated $730M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. BL Harbert International received 43 awards so far, with an average award size of $17M. BL Harbert International's obligations are down 22.2% year over year. The Department of Defense is the dominant buyer, obligating $696M. The Department of State obligated $24.6M, the Department of Justice obligated $9.5M, the General Services Administration obligated $220K, and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $10K. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest NAICS market for BL Harbert International at $681M. Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction accounted for $45.2M, and Architectural Services accounted for $4.3M. Historical totals show obligations of $488M in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $1.3B in FY23, $1B in FY24, and $938M in FY25, which provides context for the current-year pace. Current-year totals are partial and fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are BL Harbert International's largest federal customers?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $696M for BL Harbert International in FY2026 to date. The Department of State obligated $24.6M and the Department of Justice obligated $9.5M. The General Services Administration obligated $220K and the Department of Homeland Security obligated $10K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets and contract types drive BL Harbert International's federal revenue?",
        "body": "Commercial and Institutional Building Construction is the largest market at $681M. Power and Communication Line and Related Structures Construction accounted for $45.2M, and Architectural Services accounted for $4.3M. These NAICS markets together explain the majority of BL Harbert International's FY2026 to date obligations."
      }
    ]
  },
